AVM FRITZ!OS kernel - README
============================

AVM FRITZ!OS kernel is a Linux derivate.  If you want to rebuild your FRITZ!OS
kernel, exactly, please go ahead this way:

 * Enable the settings for SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, KBUILD_BUILD_USER,
   KBUILD_BUILD_HOST and KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP in .kernelvariables by setting
   'reproducibility' to a nonempty value.

 * Adjust the toolchain variables, to match your cross toolchain as required:
   CROSS_COMPILE (e.g.  mips-linux-gnu-), CC (e.g. mips-linux-gnu-gcc-5),
   HOSTCC (e.g. gcc).

 * Run 'make olddefconfig' to let kconfig regenerate the original .config file;
   remember to add 'O=../path/to/build/dir' to all make calls, if you want to
   build out-of-source.  Official FRITZ!OS kernel builds do 'olddefconfig', too,
   and with the exception of puma6 based boards, we always build out-of-source.

Now you can build the kernel almost as ususal ('make reproducibility=1 all
install modules_install headers_install dtbs_install ...').

Thanks for caring for your open-source kernel.

